# Boxfan Sensor Data Export

## Section

Export and analyze sensor readings from the boxfan device via Erlang distribution.

## Setup

Start Livebook with distribution enabled:

```
livebook server --name livebook@$(hostname).local --cookie boxfan_cookie
```

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:explorer, "~> 0.8"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.12"},
  {:kino_vega_lite, "~> 0.1"}
])

alias Explorer.DataFrame, as: DF
alias Explorer.Series

target_node = :"boxfan@boxfan.local"
```

## Connect to Device

```elixir
case Node.connect(target_node) do
  true ->
    IO.puts("Connected to #{target_node}")
    :ok

  false ->
    IO.puts("""
    Failed to connect. Make sure:
      1. boxfan has distribution enabled (requires firmware rebuild)
      2. Livebook was started with --cookie boxfan_cookie
      3. Both machines are on the same network
    """)

    :error
end
```

## Fetch Readings into DataFrame

```elixir
readings =
  :rpc.call(target_node, Data.Repo, :all, [Data.SensorReading])
  |> Enum.sort_by(& &1.inserted_at, DateTime)

df =
  DF.new(
    id: Enum.map(readings, & &1.id),
    temperature: Enum.map(readings, & &1.temperature),
    humidity: Enum.map(readings, & &1.humidity),
    pressure: Enum.map(readings, & &1.pressure),
    gas_resistance: Enum.map(readings, & &1.gas_resistance),
    inserted_at: Enum.map(readings, & &1.inserted_at)
  )

IO.puts("Loaded #{DF.n_rows(df)} readings")
df
```

## Summary Statistics

```elixir
DF.describe(df)
```

## Temperature Chart

```elixir
VegaLite.new(width: 700, height: 300, title: "Temperature Over Time")
|> VegaLite.data_from_values(df, only: ["inserted_at", "temperature"])
|> VegaLite.mark(:line)
|> VegaLite.encode_field(:x, "inserted_at", type: :temporal, title: "Time")
|> VegaLite.encode_field(:y, "temperature", type: :quantitative, title: "Temperature (°C)")
```

## Humidity Chart

```elixir
VegaLite.new(width: 700, height: 300, title: "Humidity Over Time")
|> VegaLite.data_from_values(df, only: ["inserted_at", "humidity"])
|> VegaLite.mark(:line, color: "green")
|> VegaLite.encode_field(:x, "inserted_at", type: :temporal, title: "Time")
|> VegaLite.encode_field(:y, "humidity", type: :quantitative, title: "Humidity (%)")
```

